   "id": "barnards-star",
   "title": "Barnard's Star, the fastest star",
   "description": "Barnard's Star is a small red dwarf only 6 light years away. It crosses the sky faster than any other star, about 10.4 arcseconds per year. SPHEREx saw it in August 2025 and again in May 2026.",
